Build the shell's profile-data services on HarmonyOS.

The ArkUI shell draws its own bookmark, history, download and settings
pages; chrome/browser/ui/ohos/shell_*_ohos.cc (overlay) answer its
commands from the profile. This registers those files in
//chrome/browser:core with the two deps they read directly, and hides
Chromium's download bubble when the shell draws download UI -- the same
switch an extension uses to disable download UI.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch,
ohos-system-geolocation-permission.patch, ohos-screen-orientation.patch and
ohos-shell-context-menu.patch.

